// kenergy_reality_check.dot
//
// Subgraph rendering of the "kenergy" skill (skills/kenergy/SKILL.md): a
// reality-enforcement lens with two modes -- pre-work (define what "working"
// means before an agent is dispatched) and post-work (hold a completion
// claim to that bar: proven or asserted?). Reused by build_like_ken.dot
// (pre-work, once per task, before Implement) and verify.dot (post-work,
// before the finish decision).
//
// Prompts below are ported near-verbatim from skills/kenergy/SKILL.md's
// "Output Structure" and Execution Steps -- not invented text.
//
// Inputs:
//   $mode              - "pre_work" | "post_work"
//   $task_id           - task identifier (pre_work) or claim being checked (post_work)
//   $task_description  - what the task/claim says it does
//   $claimed_evidence   - (post_work only) the evidence offered for "done"
//
// Outputs (pre_work):
//   criteria.working_definition  - one sentence: what a real user would observe
//   criteria.minimum_proof       - the specific observable demonstration required
//   criteria.verification_level - static|script|http|browser|dtu
//
// Outputs (post_work):
//   verdict.proven_or_asserted  - "proven" | "asserted"
//   verdict.gap                 - named gap if asserted, else ""

digraph kenergy_reality_check {
  graph [rankdir=LR, default_max_retry=2, default_fidelity="summary:high"];

  Start [shape=Mdiamond, label="Start"];
  Exit  [shape=Msquare,  label="Exit"];

  RouteMode [
    shape=parallelogram, label="Pre-work or Post-work?",
    tool_command="#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nprintf '%s' \"${mode}\""
  ];

  // Faithful to SKILL.md Core Behavior 1 ("Pre-Work: Define the Verification
  // Criteria") and its Output Structure.
  DefineCriteria [
    shape=box, goal_gate=true, fidelity="summary:high",
    label="Define Verification Criteria (pre-work)",
    prompt="Task: ${task_description}\n\nBefore this task is dispatched, define what \"working\" actually means -- not in terms of code written, but in terms of what a real user would observe or be able to do. \"It runs\" is not a criterion; \"a real user can do X and see Y\" is.\n\nProduce:\n- Working definition: one sentence, what a real user would observe when this is actually done.\n- Minimum proof required: the smallest demonstration that confirms the core need is met -- name the mechanism (static analysis / script execution / curl / browser / DTU).\n- What failure looks like: the specific observable sign the work has drifted.\n\nIf the verification path is genuinely uncertain, say so explicitly rather than guessing a level.\n\nWrite .resolve/build/criteria_${task_id}.json with {\"working_definition\":\"...\",\"minimum_proof\":\"...\",\"verification_level\":\"static\"|\"script\"|\"http\"|\"browser\"|\"dtu\",\"failure_looks_like\":\"...\"}. Print the single line: criteria_defined"
  ];

  // Faithful to SKILL.md Core Behavior 2 ("Post-Work: Hold the Claim to the
  // Bar") -- binary call, no hedged middle ground.
  HoldClaimToBar [
    shape=box, goal_gate=true, fidelity="summary:high",
    label="Proven or Asserted? (post-work)",
    prompt="Claim: ${task_description}\nOffered evidence: ${claimed_evidence}\n\nAsk specifically: is there real evidence here, or is this an assertion? A passing unit test is not proof of working for a non-library, real-user-facing claim. \"Should work\" is not proof. \"I tested it manually\" without a captured command and output is not proof.\n\nCall it PROVEN only if the evidence is a live run, a browser verification, a real API call, or real data -- something reproducible right now, not a theory. Otherwise call it ASSERTED and name exactly what's missing and what would satisfy it (e.g. \"no browser verify\", \"no end-to-end run\").\n\nWrite .resolve/verify/reality_check.json with {\"verdict\":\"proven\"|\"asserted\",\"gap\":\"...\"}. Print the single line: reality_checked"
  ];

  Start          -> RouteMode;
  RouteMode      -> DefineCriteria   [condition="context.tool.last_line=pre_work", weight="2"];
  RouteMode      -> HoldClaimToBar   [condition="context.tool.last_line=post_work"];
  DefineCriteria -> Exit;
  HoldClaimToBar -> Exit;
}
